=== cell 8 verdict: PASS — congested window delivered ~30 datagrams/s (matches the 300kbit bottleneck); netem qdisc stats: dropped 47, backlog 40p (bounded by limit 50); control stream stayed responsive through the whole profile (AUTH/SUBSCRIBE/UNSUBSCRIBE/CLOSE all completed, close_reason=Normal, ~1 s transport quiet during CUBIC recovery); media self-recovered to full rate (109 rx_pkts/500ms) within ~2 s of clearing, after a 633-packet burst released the queued media; gaps=1067 = 4800 sent - 3732 received exactly, duplicates=0.
=== drop accounting honesty note: the application bounded queue (cap 256) never overflowed (queue_dropped=0, no "media queue full" log lines) because send_datagram() never blocks — media drops happened in the netem qdisc (47, counted by tc -s) and inside quinn 0.11.12 internal 1 MiB datagram queue (silently evicted oldest-first, uncountable per the README-documented quinn behavior). Bounded-queue behavior is additionally covered by e2e tests (slow reader, forwarder-delay drop-newest).
